        "original_id": "c7301627-d5c7-5cf9-9391-fcfb61092837",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Making a Murderer\n- People: Steven Avery, Laura Ricciardi, Moira Demos, Penny Beerntsen\n- Companies: Netflix\n- Places: Manitowoc County, Wisconsin\n- Topics: Wrongful conviction, exoneration by DNA evidence\n\nFacts:\n- In 1985, Steven Avery, a man from Manitowoc County, Wisconsin, was wrongfully convicted of sexual assault and attempted murder.\n- Steven Avery was born on July 9, 1962.\n- In 2003, Steven Avery was fully exonerated by DNA evidence after serving 18 years in prison for the wrongful conviction involving Penny Beerntsen.\n- On December 18, 2015, Making a Murderer premiered on Netflix as an American documentary television series.\n- The first season of Making a Murderer had ten episodes.\n- Laura Ricciardi and Moira Demos wrote and directed the first season of Making a Murderer.\n- The first season of Making a Murderer explores the story of Steven Avery.",
